orms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/trees\/forest\/init(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest-path forest of a search from any number of sources, with the edges’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directions and the roots dropped: every reached vertex, in the tree’s index order as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them (unreached ones left out), and one edge (parent, child) per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached vertex with a parent, in that order. Edge positions are the forest’s own: edge k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joins the k-th listed vertex with a parent to its parent; the graph’s edge stays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tree.parentEdge(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":". O(n); the vertices are hashed once, into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forest’s lookup table, unless they are the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<k"},{"type":"text","text":" in order."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths":{"url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths","type":"topic","title":"ShortestPaths","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"}}}